# AxISA v2.2 step 2 (see docs/ISA.md's METRO section): the Metropolis
# step. GENERATED by tools/gen_metro_test.py - the expected WEIGHT bits
# in tb/tb_metro.v come from its binary32 reference model. Results are
# STOREd: weights to 0x300 + 4*i, accept counts to 0x400 + 4*i.

# WEIGHT: dS < 0: the new plaquette is better -> 1
    ADDI N1, N0, 504
    SLLI N1, N1, 11
    ORI N1, N1, 0
    SLLI N1, N1, 10
    ORI N1, N1, 0
    ADDI N2, N0, 507
    SLLI N2, N2, 11
    ORI N2, N2, 409
    SLLI N2, N2, 10
    ORI N2, N2, 614
    ADDI N3, N0, 518
    SLLI N3, N3, 11
    ORI N3, N3, 0
    SLLI N3, N3, 10
    ORI N3, N3, 0
    METRO WEIGHT, N4, N1, N2, N3
    STORE N4, N0, 0x300
